  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "A while back I made a Katamari Damacy avatar with a sphere that had a bunch of chairs on it to collect other players and roll them about. \n\nThe player would push the sphere in front of them, and it would roll forward and back, and strafe left and right as they moved, and it did this without snapping back into a default position every time the player stopped moving. \n\nI accomplished this by putting a configurable joint on the sphere, and setting the target angular velocity in the walk animations of a generic avatar. \n\nThis worked great, until the latest update. Now the sphere appears to roll locally, but remote players do not see it rotate at all. :(",
